---
import { t } from '@bool/i18n';
import BaseLayout from '@bool/ui/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalPageSection from '@bool/ui/sections/LegalPageSection.astro';
import { getHeaderLabels, getFooterLabels } from '../labels';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={t('pageMeta.cookies.title')}
  description={t('pageMeta.cookies.description')}
  headerLabels={getHeaderLabels()}
  footerLabels={getFooterLabels()}
>
  <LegalPageSection
    headingId="cookies-heading"
    ariaLabel={t('cookiesPage.heading')}
    heading={t('cookiesPage.heading')}
    subtitle={t('cookiesPage.lastUpdated')}
  >
    <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. They help the
      site remember your preferences and understand how you interact with it.
    </p>

    <h2>2. How We Use Cookies</h2>
    <p>We use cookies and similar technologies for the following purposes:</p>

    <h3>Essential Storage (No Consent Required)</h3>
    <p>These are strictly necessary for the website to function and cannot be disabled.</p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th><th>Type</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr
          ><td>theme</td><td>Stores your light/dark mode preference</td><td>Persistent</td><td
            >localStorage</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td>locale</td><td>Stores your language preference</td><td>Persistent</td><td
            >localStorage</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td>bool-consent</td><td>Stores your cookie consent preferences</td><td>365 days</td><td
            >localStorage</td
          ></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Cloudflare Turnstile may also set cookies when you interact with a form captcha. These are
      strictly necessary for bot prevention and cannot be disabled.
    </p>

    <h3>Analytics Cookies (Consent Required)</h3>
    <p>
      These help us understand how visitors use our website so we can improve it. They are only
      activated when you consent to the "Analytics" category.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th><th>Provider</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr
          ><td>_ga</td><td>Distinguishes unique users</td><td>2 years</td><td>Google Analytics</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td>_ga_*</td><td>Maintains session state</td><td>2 years</td><td>Google Analytics</td
          ></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Google Analytics is configured with IP anonymisation enabled. Analytics scripts run off the
      main thread via Partytown and are only loaded after you grant consent.
    </p>

    <h3>Error Monitoring (Consent Required)</h3>
    <p>
      We use Sentry for error monitoring, which may store technical diagnostic data. This is only
      activated when you consent to the "Analytics" category.
    </p>

    <h3>Marketing (Consent Required)</h3>
    <p>
      We do not currently use marketing cookies. This category is reserved for future use. If we
      introduce marketing cookies, this policy will be updated and your consent will be requested
      separately.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
    <p>Some cookies are placed by third-party services we use:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — analytics cookies as described above.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> — may set cookies when you interact with a form captcha.
        These are necessary for bot prevention and do not track you across sites.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Managing Your Preferences</h2>
    <p>
      You can manage your cookie preferences at any time by clicking the <strong
        >"Cookie preferences"</strong
      > link in the footer of any page. This will reopen the consent banner where you can change your
      choices.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also control cookies through your browser settings. Note that blocking all cookies may
      affect website functionality.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Consent Duration</h2>
    <p>
      Your consent preferences are stored for 365 days. After this period, you will be asked to
      consent again. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Cookie Policy to reflect changes in our practices or for legal,
      operational, or regulatory reasons. The "Last updated" date at the top indicates the most
      recent revision.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about our use of cookies, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@bool.pt"
        >info@bool.pt</a
      >.
    </p>
  </LegalPageSection>
</BaseLayout>
